#N canvas 40 60 1250 920 predict-next-note 0;
#X text 20 10 ONE PREDICTION (the trigger fires right to left: 1 -> 5). seq\$0 holds the last notes (L of them \, newest at position L-1). The QUERY is the context: the newest note c and the one before it \, p. Every earlier position j is a KEY: the notes just before it \, seq[j-1] and seq[j-2]. Its VALUE is seq[j] \, the note that followed that context., f 170;
#X obj 20 80 inlet;
#X obj 20 106 t b b b b b;
#X text 700 150 1) the query: c = newest note \, p = the note before it, f 70;
#X obj 60 150 expr seq\$0[L_\$0 - 1] \; seq\$0[L_\$0 - 2];
#X obj 400 150 v c_\$0;
#X obj 400 174 v pv_\$0;
#X text 700 216 2) a SCORE for every earlier position j = 1 .. L-1: how well seq[j-1] matches c (weight 4) and seq[j-2] matches p (weight = context) \, minus a little for older positions (recency). Positions that do not exist get -1000 (never chosen)., f 70;
#X obj 60 210 t b;
#X obj 60 236 t b b;
#X msg 120 262 0;
#X msg 60 262 32;
#X obj 60 288 until;
#X obj 60 314 f;
#X obj 110 314 + 1;
#X obj 60 346 expr sc\$0[\$f1] = if(\$f1 >= 1 && \$f1 <= L_\$0 - 1 \, -4 * abs(seq\$0[\$f1 - 1] - c_\$0) / 12 - ctx_\$0 * (\$f1 >= 2) * abs(seq\$0[\$f1 - 2] - pv_\$0) / 12 - rec_\$0 * (L_\$0 - 1 - \$f1) \, -1000), f 80;
#X text 700 470 3) softmax(score / T) -> the attention weights att\$0. They add up to 1 (a probability distribution)., f 70;
#X obj 60 470 nn.softmax sc\$0 att\$0;
#X obj 300 444 r \$0-temp;
#X text 700 530 4) SAMPLE a position from the weights: draw r between 0 and 1 \, add up the weights from the left and count how many running sums stay below r. That count is the chosen position (inverse CDF sampling)., f 70;
#X obj 60 530 t b b b;
#X obj 400 560 random 10000;
#X obj 400 586 / 10000;
#X obj 400 612 v r_\$0;
#X msg 560 560 0;
#X obj 560 586 v cum_\$0;
#X obj 640 586 v cnt_\$0;
#X obj 60 640 t b b;
#X msg 120 666 0;
#X msg 60 666 32;
#X obj 60 692 until;
#X obj 60 718 f;
#X obj 110 718 + 1;
#X obj 60 750 t f f;
#X obj 200 776 expr cum_\$0 + att\$0[\$f1];
#X obj 200 802 v cum_\$0;
#X obj 60 830 expr cnt_\$0 + (cum_\$0 < r_\$0);
#X obj 60 856 v cnt_\$0;
#X text 700 860 5) COPY: the prediction is the note that followed the chosen moment \, seq[chosen]. Append it (and play it)., f 70;
#X obj 400 860 expr seq\$0[min(cnt_\$0 \, 31)];
#X obj 400 886 s \$0-append;
